  {:name "hich44" :created "2013-02-04 04:06" :body "<p>mercie pour ce sujet interessant moi aussi jutilise cet appareil eller super mais je veut augmenter la porter de la reception wifi de mon appareil es que je peut ajouter ce tipe dantenne tp-link wifi externe grille parabolique Gain de 24dB et la souder sur mon appareil comme vous avez fait</p>" :children []}
  {:name "Diarmaid Ó Cualain (@DiarDan)" :created "2013-03-21 21:23" :body "<p>I came across this antenna modification and a similar specified one on the OpenWRT forums. I performed the mod, but was disappointed with the antenna gain. By comparing the performance of my Buffalo router and the TP 703n using the same antenna, there was nearly a 50% improvement in signal quality from the Buffalo.</p><p>However, I believe you were more on track with your first modification , a link to which you gave at the beginning of the blog post. If you cut the trace to the internal antenna, as specified in your first modification, leave C114 as it is, and then solder the coax of the external antenna to either end of the J1 0 ohm resistor, you should get better gain performance.</p><p>By removing the j1 0 ohm resistor, you not only are removing the internal antenna from the circuit (which is a good thing, if you want to connect an external antenna), but you are also removing C29 C31 (beside the internal antenna). I believe this is the reason for the drop in signal quality.</p><p>I have noticed now that my TP 703n router has comparable performance to my buffalo router using the same external antenna. I hope this helps!</p>" :children [ {:name "Stian Eikeland" :created "2013-03-26 13:29" :body "<p>This is certainly interesting, I will try to bridge j1 again and see if I there is a difference in signal strength.<br>Thank you :)</p>" :children [ {:name "darkside40" :created "2013-05-08 18:01" :body "<p>Interesting mod. Did you already had the chance to check if bridging J1 and cutting the internal antenna gives you a better signal strenght?</p>" :children [ {:name "Stian Eikeland" :created "2013-05-15 21:58" :body "<p>Sadly haven't had time yet :/<br>Please let me know if you (or anyone else) try.</p>" :children []}]} {:name "hoschisubs" :created "2013-05-09 18:21" :body "<p>Did you already had any time to try this?</p>" :children []}]}]}
  {:name "Valent Turkovic" :created "2013-04-02 12:57" :body "<p>Hi, this is awesome mod. <br>I have wrote about your antenna connector mod on openwrt forum and wiki:<br><a href=\"https://forum.openwrt.org/viewtopic.php?pid=196933#p196933\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://forum.openwrt.org/v...</a></p>" :children []}
  {:name "P Harrison" :created "2013-06-17 19:48" :body "<p>Does this mod increase signal if you are using it as a 4G router? Is the antenna specific to the wifi only?</p>" :children [ {:name "Stian Eikeland" :created "2013-06-17 19:49" :body "<p>Only helps with wifi</p>" :children [ {:name "P Harrison" :created "2013-06-18 04:54" :body "<p>Thought that might be the case. Thanks.</p><p>Guess I'll be cracking open the 4G USB modem I have on order. If I find the antenna location I'll post it here.</p><p>~P</p>" :children []}]}]}
